<title>CHINA: Tse Sui Luen says two directors resign.</title>
<headline>Tse Sui Luen says two directors resign.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tse Sui Luen Jewellery (International) Ltd said two of its non-executive directors resigned with effect from July 21, following the sale of Yue Xiu Finance Co's 11 percent stake in the company to Union Bank of Switzerland.</p>
<p>The jewellery company said in a statement that Mai Yifeng and Wang Shiming were appointed as directors in 1993 and 1995 respectively.</p>
<p>It did not name any replacements for them.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
